MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> what if I would like to judge whether the predicted intercept or slope will deviate from certain values (for example, 0 or any other values) when cov1 and cov2 were fixed at some values. Could I do this in Lavaan?

You can center Cov1 and Cov2 at different (combinations of) values to test significance conditional on those levels.  Then you fit the model to those re-centered covariates.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

